# MiniShipSim hull -- low-poly, closed, symmetric
# object Hull / mesh HullMesh
#
# Frame: +X = bow, +Y = port (starboard = -Y), +Z = up. Units: metres.
# Origin: still-water line, amidships (x=0), on the centreline (y=0).
# Axes are Blender-native and were exported without any rotation:
#   forward=+Y, up=+Z is the identity mapping, so OBJ coords == Blender coords.
#   Blender's default (-Z forward, Y up) would instead map (x,y,z)->(x,z,-y),
#   putting the beam on Z and the deck height on Y. Not used here.
# Principal dimensions: LOA 4.000 m, beam 1.500 m, draft 0.280 m, freeboard 0.495 m, depth 0.775 m
# Faces are written as polygons (quads and two 10-gon caps), one per line.

o Hull
